values ('a5e8c2d7-1b49-4f06-9a31-6d0c3e8b5f17', 'nutrition-counseling-and-education', 'Nutrition Counseling and Education', 'This advanced undergraduate course develops evidence-informed nutrition counseling, education, and communication skills for diverse individuals and groups. Students integrate person-centered communication, motivational interviewing, behavior-change theory, the Nutrition Care Process, cultural humility, structural context, health literacy, instructional design, group facilitation, digital communication, eating-disorder safety, telehealth, documentation, and evaluation. Repeated simulations and feedback build observable competence in listening, assessment, shared agenda setting, information exchange, action planning, teach-back, group teaching, referral, and professional documentation. The course prepares students for supervised dietetics practice; it does not confer independent clinical or psychotherapy scope.');

